  "term": "anticipatory pleasure",
  "definition": "Anticipatory pleasure is the expected positive feeling a person thinks they will have during an upcoming experience. In this packet, so-called deficits in anticipatory pleasure are described as possibly reflecting stronger expectation of negative emotion, rather than simply reduced expectation of positive emotion.",
